hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20797","Abd al-Razzaq told us, Sufyan informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, from al-Ashath ibn Thurmulah, from Abu Bakrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a covenanted soul without its right, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has forbidden him Paradise, that he smell its scent."
"20798","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi told us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad, then he mentioned a story in it, he said: When he arrived, Abdullah was given a choice between thirty thousand and vessels of silver. He said: So he chose the vessels. He said: Then merchants from Darin came and he sold them to them, ten for thirteen. Then he met Abu Bakrah and said: Did you not see how I deceived them? He said: How? So he mentioned that to him. He said: I adjure you, or I swear upon you, that you return it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding the like of this."
"21364","Umar ibn Ubayd Abu Hafs narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, After me there will be twelve commanders, he said, Then he spoke and what he said was hidden from me, he said, So I asked some of the people, or the one next to me, What did he say, he said, All of them are from Quraysh."
"21365","Umar ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said, I never saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, preaching except standing."
"23993","Yunus ibn Muhammad and Hujayn both said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Asim ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi, that they raided the raid of al-Salasil, and the raid escaped them, so they remained stationed, then returned to Mu'awiyah, with Abu Ayyub and Uqbah ibn Amir with him. Asim said: O Abu Ayyub, the raid escaped us this year, and we were informed that whoever prays in the mosque, and Hujayn said: the four mosques, his sin is forgiven. He said: Nephew, shall I guide you to easier than that? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever performs ablution as commanded and prays as commanded, what he did before is forgiven. Is it so, O Uqbah? He said: Yes."
"23994","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'a narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub al-Ansari, he narrated to him, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Conceal the proposal, then perform ablution and perfect your ablution, and pray what Allah has written for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O Allah, You decree and I do not decree, and You know and I do not know, You are Knower of the unseen. If You see good for me in so-and-so, naming her by her name, in my religion, my world, and my hereafter, and if another than her is better for me than her in my religion, my world, and my hereafter, decree her for me, or he said: ordain her for me."
"23995","Harun narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Haywah informed me, that al-Walid ibn al-Walid informed him, and he mentioned it with its chain and meaning: one hundred and twelve hadiths."
"24079","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, and he was among the companions of al-Saqifah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Not of righteousness is fasting in travel, in the dialect: Laysa min ambrr amsiyam fi amsafar."
"24305","Husayn narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abis, from Farwah ibn Musayk, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard a man saying: O Messenger of Allah, is Saba a land or a woman, he said: It is neither a land nor a woman, but it is a man who fathered ten of the Arabs, four of them went to the left and six went to the right, as for those who went to the left: Akk, Lakhm, Ghassan, and Amilah, and as for those who went to the right: al-Azd, Kindah, Madhhij, Himyar, al-Ash'ariyyun, and Anmar, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is Anmar, he said: Those from whom are Khath'am and Bajilah."
"24306","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah al-Kalbi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hani ibn Urwah, from Farwah ibn Musayk, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I fight with those of my people who come forward against those of them who turn away, he said: Yes, so fight with those who come forward against those who turn away, then when I turned away he called me and said: Do not fight them until you call them to Islam, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about Saba, is it a valley or a mountain, he said: No, rather it is a man of the Arabs, to whom ten were born, six went to the right and four went to the left: to the right went al-Azd, al-Ash'ariyyun, Himyar, Kindah, Madhhij, and Anmar, those of whom are said to be Bajilah and Khath'am, and to the left went Lakhm, Judham, Amilah, and Ghassan."
"24307","Abdullah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakha'i narrated to me, Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i informed us, from Farwah ibn Musayk al-Ghutayfi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not fight whoever turns away of my people with whoever of them comes forward, he said: Yes, then it occurred to me and I said: O Messenger of Allah, no, rather the people of Saba, for they are mightier and stronger, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me and permitted me to fight them, then when I left him Allah revealed concerning Saba what He revealed, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What happened to al-Ghutayfi, so he sent to my dwelling and found that I had set out, so I was brought back, and when I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I found him sitting with his Companions, and he said: Rather call the people, whoever answers accept from him, and whoever does not answer do not hasten against him until you refer to me, a man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Saba, is it a land or a woman, he said: It is neither a land nor a woman, but it is a man who fathered ten of the Arabs, six of them went to the right and four went to the left, as for those who went to the left: Lakhm, Judham, Ghassan, and Amilah, and as for those who went to the right: al-Uzd, Kindah, Himyar, al-Ash'ariyyun, Anmar, and Madhhij, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is Anmar, he said: Those from whom are Khath'am and Bajilah."
"24308","Abdullah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam narrated to me, Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Farwah ibn Musayk al-Ghutayfi, then al-Muradi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned its meaning."
"27150","[Source text truncated in index: Haddathana]"
